      ],
      "reproduction": "_prepare always puts the explicit SB at ordered_ids[0] and BB at ordered_ids[1]; for two players _positions says index 0 is BB and index 1 is BTN. A local PokerKit state probe created with blinds [SB, BB] and two unknown hole cards reports bets [BB, SB] and first actor index 1. Mapped to ordered_ids [SB, BB], that index is the source BB, while a real heads-up preflop source first action is by the SB/button. The converter will misassign blind stacks/positions and reject that first action as engine_action_order_mismatch (or produce wrong postflop actor mapping).",
      "reproduction_file": "data/acquisition_resume/2026-11-01/converter_review/heads-up-order-probe.py",
      "reviewed_source_example": "No Ivey heads-up source hand is present in sample-final-table or the three inspected 2023 hands (each has three players), so impact was not demonstrated on a saved Ivey candidate.",
      "row_specific_impact": "Does not affect the seven-handed candidate reviewed above.",
      "severity": "high",
      "title": "Heads-up seat ordering conflicts with PokerKit\u2019s heads-up blind order"
    },
    {
      "code_locations": [
        "scripts/acquisition_triton_convert.py:493-501",
        "scripts/acquisition_triton_convert.py:591-593",
        "scripts/acquisition_triton_convert.py:665-674"
      ],
      "reproduction": "The loop drops round_index/action_index and increments one flat counter across all rounds. A postflop action therefore receives a hand-global number rather than its source round-local action index; output omits round_index. This conflicts with the requested raw UUID + original round/action index identity and makes row-to-source traceability less direct.",
      "reviewed_source_example": "All emitted/inspected Ivey actions in the reviewed sample are preflop; sample candidate round 0 action 6 happens to equal flattened index 6. The 2023 examples are also preflop hero actions and emit no rows, so no current candidate is mislabeled by this issue.",
